{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3017","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3017","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3017\",\"parent_revision\":\"09c35031873e81490e1fbe109087743a89f52cd3efb4d027f1cff3ce70388481\",\"root_revision\":\"09c35031873e81490e1fbe109087743a89f52cd3efb4d027f1cff3ce70388481\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFound during PR #3008 review/fix (the scheduled main-CI-health-check workflow, issue #3001). The tracking-issue lookup in `.github/workflows/main-ci-health-check.yml` only searches `state: 'open'` for an existing tracking issue. Sequence that breaks:\\n\\n1. Main goes red \u2192 workflow opens tracking issue #N.\\n2. Main goes green \u2192 workflow closes #N with an all-clear comment.\\n3. Main goes red again \u2192 workflow searches only open issues, finds none, opens a **new** issue #M instead of reopening #N.\\n\\nThis contradicts the workflow's own stated design (a single persistent, reused tracking issue) and produces issue-list noise proportional to how often main flips red/green.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Tracking-issue lookup also finds a previously-closed issue matching the tracking label/title and reopens it instead of creating a new one, OR the design is deliberately changed (with rationale) to open genuinely new issues per red-cycle\\n- [ ] A test/validation harness (see the mocked-API approach used in PR #3008's fix, `.tmp/scratch/tests/validate_main_ci_health_check.py` pattern) covers the reopen-vs-duplicate-create behavior explicitly\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer relying on the main-CI-health tracking issue**, I want to **one persistent issue reused across red/green cycles**, so that **I don't get duplicate issues for the same recurring problem**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Found by a review agent on PR #3008, confirmed by the fix agent, deliberately left unfixed there to avoid scope creep \u2014 see PR #3008 for the surrounding context and the workflow file this applies to.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"23a21cdaa322189b790857108aa7e6ad018b31cff539a1e3b77573eb393f64dc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiIerA\"}"}